  {
   "id": 0,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 1924,
   "end": 1933,
   "text": "# OpenArm",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 1935,
   "end": 2051,
   "text": "[OpenArm](⟦0⟧) is an open-source 7DOF humanoid arm designed for physical AI research and deployment.",
   "tokens": [
    "https://openarm.dev"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 2053,
   "end": 2215,
   "text": "To get your OpenArm, assembled or DIY, and join the global community, browse verified and certified manufacturers worldwide at [openarm.dev](⟦0⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "https://openarm.dev"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 2217,
   "end": 2234,
   "text": "## What's Unique?",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2236,
   "end": 2465,
   "text": "- **Human-Scale Design**: OpenArm is designed with human-like proportions, scaled for a person around 160-165cm tall. This provides an optimal balance between practical reach and manageable inertia for safe, responsive operation.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2467,
   "end": 2704,
   "text": "- **Safety-First Architecture**: Built with QDD backdrivable motors and high compliance, OpenArm prioritizes safe human-robot interaction while maintaining practical payload capabilities (6.0kg peak / 4.1kg nominal) for real-world tasks.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2706,
   "end": 2899,
   "text": "- **Built for Durability**: Critical structural components use aluminum and stainless steel construction, ensuring robust performance for repetitive data collection and continuous research use.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 2901,
   "end": 3133,
   "text": "- **Fully Accessible & Buildable**: Every component, from CNC parts and 3D-printed casings to electrical wiring is designed to be purchasable and buildable by individual researchers and labs, with complete fabrication data provided.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3135,
   "end": 3306,
   "text": "- **Practical & Affordable**: At $6,500 USD for a complete bimanual system, OpenArm delivers research-grade capabilities at a fraction of traditional humanoid robot costs.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3308,
   "end": 3332,
   "text": "## Platform Requirements",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3334,
   "end": 3501,
   "text": "⟦0⟧\n  **Linux Only**: OpenArm currently only works on Linux. The CAN bus USB adapter\n  does not have macOS drivers and has not been tested on Windows.",
   "tokens": [
    "<Tip warning={true}>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 3510,
   "end": 3525,
   "text": "## Safety Guide",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 3527,
   "end": 3660,
   "text": "Before operating OpenArm, please read the [official safety guide](⟦0⟧). Key points:",
   "tokens": [
    "https://docs.openarm.dev/getting-started/safety-guide"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3662,
   "end": 3751,
   "text": "- **Secure installation**: Fasten the arm to a flat, stable surface with screws or clamps",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3752,
   "end": 3845,
   "text": "- **Safe distance**: Keep body parts and objects outside the range of motion during operation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3846,
   "end": 3930,
   "text": "- **Protective equipment**: Always wear safety goggles; use additional PPE as needed",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 16,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 3931,
   "end": 4028,
   "text": "- **Payload limits**: Do not exceed specified payload limits (6.0kg peak / 4.1kg nominal per arm)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 17,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4029,
   "end": 4111,
   "text": "- **Emergency stop**: Know the location and operation of the emergency stop device",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 18,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4112,
   "end": 4222,
   "text": "- **Regular inspection**: Check for loose screws, damaged mechanical limits, unusual noises, and wiring damage",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 19,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4224,
   "end": 4241,
   "text": "## Hardware Setup",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 20,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4243,
   "end": 4326,
   "text": "Follow the official [OpenArm hardware documentation](⟦0⟧) for:",
   "tokens": [
    "https://docs.openarm.dev"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 21,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4328,
   "end": 4360,
   "text": "- Bill of materials and sourcing",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 22,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4361,
   "end": 4387,
   "text": "- 3D printing instructions",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 23,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4388,
   "end": 4409,
   "text": "- Mechanical assembly",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 24,
   "kind": "list",
   "start": 4410,
   "end": 4429,
   "text": "- Electrical wiring",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 25,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4431,
   "end": 4539,
   "text": "The hardware repositories are available at [github.com/enactic/openarm](⟦0⟧).",
   "tokens": [
    "https://github.com/enactic/openarm"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 26,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4541,
   "end": 4557,
   "text": "## CAN Bus Setup",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 27,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4559,
   "end": 4762,
   "text": "OpenArm uses CAN bus communication with Damiao motors. Once you have the CAN bus USB adapter plugged into your Linux PC, follow the [Damiao Motors and CAN Bus guide](⟦0⟧) to configure the interface.",
   "tokens": [
    "./damiao"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 28,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4764,
   "end": 4776,
   "text": "Quick setup:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 29,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 4949,
   "end": 4969,
   "text": "## Install LeRobot 🤗",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 30,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 4971,
   "end": 5058,
   "text": "Follow our [Installation Guide](⟦0⟧), then install the Damiao motor support:",
   "tokens": [
    "./installation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": 31,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5100,
   "end": 5108,
   "text": "## Usage",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 32,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 5110,
   "end": 5134,
   "text": "### Follower Arm (Robot)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 6047,
   "end": 6076,
   "text": "### Leader Arm (Teleoperator)",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 6078,
   "end": 6168,
   "text": "The leader arm is used for teleoperation - manually moving it to control the follower arm.",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 6823,
   "end": 6840,
   "text": "### Teleoperation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 6842,
   "end": 6894,
   "text": "To teleoperate OpenArm with leader-follower control:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 7131,
   "end": 7157,
   "text": "### Bimanual Teleoperation",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 38,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7159,
   "end": 7237,
   "text": "To teleoperate a bimanual OpenArm setup with two leader and two follower arms:",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 39,
   "kind": "heading",
   "start": 7670,
   "end": 7688,
   "text": "### Recording Data",
   "tokens": []
  },
  {
   "id": 40,
   "kind": "para",
   "start": 7690,
   "end": 7731,
   "text": "To record a dataset during teleoperation:",
   "tokens": []
  },
